Reviewed Git pushes

Install:
  Install the missing bundled skill, required git-review and git-commit skills, and Git; preserve installed skill files.

Upgrade:
  Back up and replace the installed git-push skill with bundled files; restore previous skill files if replacement fails.

Status:
  Report git-push and required skill locations based on SKILL.md presence and the Git command location and version.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.

Configuration:
  Destination: ~/.agents/skills/git-push
  Existing copies at ${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/skills/git-push are consolidated into links to the destination when skill files are replaced.
  Required skills: git-review and git-commit; installed when missing, with upgrades managed by their own modules.
  Pending changes are reviewed and committed before pushing; a clean worktree is pushed directly.
  Remote authentication and branch permissions must already allow the requested push.
